{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"6f406eedc9ccb340b050d5bb23601a9d2d6c00514f35d17bff6c00dfb9c4ec66","digest":{"component_or_area":"CI workflows","key_entities":[".github/workflows/test.yml",".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml",".pre-commit-config.yaml","tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py","SKIP env variable","pre-commit run --all-files","make lint","make typecheck"],"problem_keywords":["CI optimization","redundant execution","pre-commit hooks","lint","typecheck","double-run"],"propositions":["The lint and typecheck hooks are executed twice in CI: once as direct steps (make lint, make typecheck) and again when pre-commit run --all-files re-invokes them.","The CI pre-commit SKIP environment variable should include 'lint' and 'typecheck' (in addition to 'no-commit-to-branch') to prevent the redundant re-run.","Both test.yml and gerrit-verify.yaml workflows must apply identical SKIP configurations for consistency.","The lint and typecheck hooks must remain in .pre-commit-config.yaml so local git commit still runs them; only the CI re-run should be skipped.","A regression guard test must verify that CI pre-commit correctly skips lint and typecheck to prevent silent reintroduction of the double-run."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787292968725072001,"uuid":"50f8f5c7-6d9e-46b6-963a-b5e97f0c5560"}